 **Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
-- **Precision:** The calculation of $s$ involves division by $1+t$. Since $t \ge 0$, $1+t \ge 1$, so division by zero is avoided [S1, unofficial].
-- **Boundary Conditions:** The `inner_mask` must correctly identify the last segment of each ray. Including the last segment in the middle weight sum would incorrectly double-count its contribution relative to the background blending term [G].
-- **Memory/Contiguity:** The `index_add_` operation requires the output tensor to be contiguous. Initializing with `torch.zeros` ensures this [G].
